cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cohaera: session-scoped security verdicts for agent telemetry"
message: >-
  If you use Cohaera in academic work, please cite it. Please also cite the
  version and the evaluation card digest: the numbers move between versions and
  a citation without them is not reproducible.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hafeez
    given-names: Imran
repository-code: "https://github.com/404SecNotFound/Cohaera"
abstract: >-
  Cohaera is a correlation layer for AI agent telemetry. It turns a flat
  per-event stream into session-scoped verdicts a SIEM can fire rules on, and
  reports what it could not evaluate, because a check that silently cannot run
  is a false negative wearing a green tick. It is dependency-free, offline, and
  ships an evaluation card that reports its false-positive rate and a catalogue
  of the ways its checks can be defeated.
keywords:
  - agent security
  - LLM agents
  - detection engineering
  - telemetry
  - SIEM
  - prompt injection
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
